<header class="hero">
<p class="kicker">A working tool for wet-road physics</p>
<h1>Hydroplaning: when water lifts a tire</h1>
<p class="lede">At speed on a wet road, water pressure in front of a tire can grow until it carries the tire's entire load. Contact — and with it steering and braking — is lost. This tool derives that onset speed from first principles, checks it against NASA's experiments, and lets you test it yourself with the calculator below.</p>
</header>

<div class="card" role="img" aria-label="Diagram of a tire meeting a water film: a wedge of water builds ahead of the contact patch and lifts the tire">
